\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For uniform odd integer Lipschitz heights on triangular-lattice approximations of a smooth simply connected planar domain with the stated two-arc boundary data, does the height distribution converge to the harmonic boundary extension plus sigma times the domain GFF, for a universal $\sigma >0$, with convergence of every joint test-function moment and mean?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For uniform odd integer Lipschitz heights on triangular-lattice approximations of a smooth simply connected planar domain with the stated two-arc boundary data, does the height distribution converge to the harmonic boundary extension plus sigma times the domain GFF, for a universal $\sigma >0$, with convergence of every joint test-function moment and mean?

